    excerpt: "OpenOcean is an early-stage venture capital firm investing in B2B software across Europe with offices in London & Helsinki. OpenOcean is a pan-European early-stage venture capital investor. Our DNA is rooted in having a deep understanding of the underlying technology and software stacks, which drive the growth of innovative new digital platforms and services. Our strong technical background and global scaling expertise allows us to identify and invest in the category winning start-ups at the early-stages, whose unique solutions can be rapidly scaled and adopted globally. OpenOcean in the press Sifted Deeptech VCs are still too risk-averse with spinouts, and it’s costing them, say Europe’s leading spinout investors Deeptech is taking a bigger share of Europe's early-stage cheques than ever. University spinouts are still getting a sliver of it. Four investors who back them explain why, and how they deal with the challenges. Founded by the entrepreneurs who sold their previous start-up to estate agent Dexters, Supa has landed a seed funding round which will help expand their property management venture, Sky News understands. Measures include a 10% capital gains rate for founders, higher employee share option limits and visa changes. Ubitium is developing a universal processor that combines sensing, AI inference and real-time control to simplify computing for autonomous machines, with plans to advance its first commercial chip towards production. With a trio of co-leads from arou",
