    sourceUrl: "https://www.gic.com.sg/",
    sourceDate: "2026-11-20",
    excerpt: "We are driven by a common purpose – securing Singapore’s financial future. GIC does not provide investment services to the public. If anyone offers you investment services using GIC's name or brand, do not reply or click on any links. Find out more . Wealthsimple raises $425 million led by GIC at $13.8 billion valuation to accelerate growth Opening Remarks by GIC CEO Lim Chow Kiat at the Opening of The Secret Vault, GIC’s First Public Exhibition GIC is a global long-term investor established in 1981 to manage Singapore’s foreign reserves. We are invested in more than 40 countries worldwide. For more than 40 years, GIC has worked to secure Singapore's financial future by preserving and enhancing the nation's reserves, for generations to come. GIC manages Singapore’s foreign reserves, with a mandate to preserve and enhance Singapore's international purchasing power over the long term. We work seamlessly as one GIC, united in the common pursuit of investing for Singapore’s future. Keep abreast of GIC’s insights on recent market developments and stay updated on key investment trends. What if intelligence became scalable and plentiful, or AI progress stalled? At GIC Insights 2026, GIC CEO Lim Chow Kiat explored two ‘what ifs’ that matter to investors and why AI investing comes down to what is already priced in. A changing world order, AI, and fiscal risks are converging to reshape investing. We assess what these macro forces mean for growth, inflation, and rates, and how long-term",
    note: "",
    logo: "/logos/gic.png",
    synthetic: false,
    confirmed: false,
    currency: "GBP",
    files: [{"title": "Company", "text": "Established in 1981 to manage Singapore's foreign reserves, we strive to achieve good long-term real returns on assets under our management to preserve and enhance the value of Singapore's reserves. We have investments in over 40 countries and are headquartered in Singapore, with 11 offices in key financial cities worldwide. “Less exciting, but reliable” was once a common perception of transport infrastructure, such as ports, toll roads and airports. But the energy transition is reshaping this asset class, introducing new technology and policy considerations for investors. GIC’s Kamil Burganov , Senior Vice President, Infrastructure (Europe), shares his perspective on the importance of adapting to the transition as it unfolds, rather than betting on a single technology. #gic #gicsg Which conversation from GIC Insights 2026 should we bring to you? Vote below and we will share key insights on your selected topic after the event. As we mark 40 years in the Bay Area, this year’s GIC Insights will be travelling to San Francisco under the theme \"What If\", bringing together founders, investors, industry leaders, and policymakers for candid discussions"}],

