    stage: "Seed",
    round: null,
    summary: "Give your agents access to the whole web. From login to task completion, Browserbase powers agents that reliably operate on the web. Web search, built for agents. Let your Agent quickly find relevant websites based on a single query. Quickly fetch web context for your agent by converting any URL into HTML, JSON or markdown Give your agent a real browser to use the web like a human. Navigating interactive website and performing complex actions, without interruptions. Send your agent to search, organize, and act on data while you do literally anything else. Run agents that click through your product continuously and alert you the moment something breaks. Job applications, vendor portals, government forms. Agents that act on the web, not just read it. Upload files, trigger downloads, and process records across hundreds of sites in parallel. Email Password Verified Captcha passed Authenticated Zero setup. Real results. Spin up a browser, connect your model, and execute your first task Spin up a browser instance, configure your environment, and prepare it to run tasks across the web. Connect AI to the browser session so it can interpret pages, make decisions, and drive interactions autonomously. Run your first workflow end-to-end, from navigation to action, and see results directly in the browser. Talk to sales Don’t use the web. Scale it. Don’t use the web. human years browsing the web",
    person: null,
    funder: "",
    source: "Company site",
    sourceUrl: "https://www.browserbase.com/",
    files: [{"title": "About", "text": "We build the infrastructure that connects AI to the web, so agents can take on repetitive online work and people can focus on what matters to them. The work that matters still happens in websites, portals, and forms built for humans. We give AI agents the tools to work in those systems on people’s behalf. Founded by Paul Klein IV in 2024, Browserbase builds the infrastructure that connects AI to the web. Our goal is to let software handle repetitive online work, so people can spend their time on what matters to them. Build with Stagehand, our open source browser automation framework, and run on Browserbase with session replays, logs, and live views to see what your agents do. Our $40 million Series B, announced in June 2025, was led by Notable Capital with participation from CRV and Kleiner Perkins. Together, we’re building the infrastructure for a web that agents can use. We care about customers, take ownership, and build the infrastructure behind a new generation of software. If you want to help agents do useful work on the web, join us."}],

