    summary: "is an applied research lab in San Francisco founded in 2025 by Div Garg, Steve Frey and Naman Garg. It builds AGI-0, AGI Agent and AGI-RUN. ')\"> ')\"> ')\"> ')\"> An applied research lab building action AI AI should do things for you, not just chat. We do original research on models that act, and we ship them as products: AGI-ACT, a small action model, AGI Agent, which works across any app, and AGI-RUN, an inference engine that runs it at the edge. Our family of small action models, from 2B to 20B+ parameters. AGI-0 scores 100% on AndroidWorld, 116 of 116 tasks. The assistant built on AGI-0. It sees the screen, reasons, and acts across any app. No integrations, no APIs. Our inference engine for phones, laptops, and edge hardware. Up to 9.9x faster than state-of-the-art engines, winning 58 of 60 benchmark cases. CEO and Co-founder. Previously founded MultiOn, the first company to deploy computer-use agents in the browser. Adjunct CS professor at Stanford; created the first course on Transformers (10M+ views) and co-taught with Andrew Ng. 3K research citations and 10 patents in AI. Co-founder & President. Previously founded a fintech scaled to $500M AUM. Research at Stanford and Berkeley. Founding research at Eon, which collected the world's largest connectomics dataset, and at Kernel, a neurotech hardware lab.",
