    stage: "Seed",
    round: null,
    summary: "Plausible is a lightweight and open-source Google Analytics alternative. Your website data is 100% yours and the privacy of your visitors is respected. Loads fast and won't affect your page speed or Core Web Vitals. A fraction of the size of Google Analytics. The code is public and auditable. Verify exactly what we collect, and run it yourself if you want to. Google Analytics is overkill for most site owners. Plausible gives you clear, useful insights without complexity, training or prior analytics experience. Google Analytics is frustrating to use, difficult to understand, slow to load and privacy-invasive. That's why we built Plausible Analytics, a simple, privacy-first alternative that doesn't cut corners. Here's what makes Plausible a great Google Analytics alternative and why over 22,000 paying customers trust us with their website and business insights: Plausible is simple web analytics . It is easy to understand and cuts through the noise. Check your site traffic and get the essential insights on one page in one minute. Get an aggregated view of all your sites in a consolidated dashboard. There are no layers of menus and no need to build custom reports, custom dashboards or PowerPoint documents. You can even import your Google Analytics stats. We invite you to take a look around, explore our live demo and try Plausible for free. We'd be honored to have you as a customer. Thank you. P.S. We're a completely independent, self-funded, bootstrapped and profitable team of 11",
    person: null,
    funder: "",
    source: "Company site",
    sourceUrl: "https://plausible.io/",
    files: [{"title": "About", "text": "Uku Taht started Plausible in December 2018, building it alone as a simple privacy-friendly alternative to Google Analytics. In 2020, when it was still just Uku building and a few hundred paying customers, Marko Saric joined to handle marketing and communications. The company has grown through product improvement and transparent communication ever since. Plausible crossed $1 million in annual recurring revenue in 2022 and has continued to grow as a profitable, independently operated company. We are self-funded and profitable, with no outside investors and no plans to sell. We do not sell or share customer data and we do not monetize visitor behavior. More than 2,400 teams have been paying for Plausible for five years or longer. Their continued support helps us build an independent business for the long term. We have never spent a cent on advertising, affiliates or paid endorsements. Plausible grows because people recommend it when they have no reason to other than that it works."}],

