    stage: "",
    round: null,
    summary: "Slite connects to the tools where work happens to build and maintain the knowledge your business depends on, so your team and their AI can work from reliable answers. Slite builds and maintains the knowledge your business depends on, so your team and their AI work from reliable answers. Talk to us Th The Nice Co. Agent Search Agent triage Channels Company Help Center Getting Started Features Troubleshooting Compliance Engineering Product People & Ops Help Center / Troubleshooting Share Verified Self-maintained Troubleshooting Common issues and how to fix them. Make sure you're using the email address tied to your Slite workspace. Reset your password from the login page if needed. Try a hard refresh (Cmd+Shift+R) or clear your browser cache. If the issue persists, try a different browser. Re-index your workspace from Settings → Advanced → Reindex. Results update within a few minutes. Check that notifications are enabled in Settings → Notifications and that Slite isn't blocked by your browser or OS. Slite rewrites outdated documentation on autopilot Slite Agent watches Slack, Linear, GitHub and your codebase, spots outdated facts in your documentation, and drafts the update for you to approve in one click. Sales No more pitching last year's features. Pricing and playbooks update with every release. Teams build from requirements that changed last quarter. Slite keeps product documentation and release notes current. Slite Agent drafts the change and sends it to the document owner",
    person: null,
    funder: "",
    source: "Company site",
    sourceUrl: "https://slite.com/",
    files: [{"title": "About", "text": "In 2025, we went multi product and built its cousin, Super, for the AI era. Super is teams' ultimate AI search on all their tools, and a way for them to accelerate all their workflows with agents able to tap on their collective knowledge. We care deeply about our work and trust our teammates to do the same. We care about our customers, about shipping only greatness, and about our impact on the community. The best way to build strong relationships in any workplace is to do meaningful work. Remote requires you to promote yourself and your work more than you may be used to. Don't be afraid to speak up, repeat yourself, and ask others to amplify your voice. We are not afraid to cross boundaries and to get things done when they need to be. If something is broken, we fix it rather than complain. “We build Slite for the long run, always looking at the impact we have on our team and the people who use Slite, as well as the broader world.” — Christophe Pasquier, Slite CEO. Our commitment is not just empty words - we measure our impact in tons of CO2 per work"}],

