    logo: "/logos/vinted.png",
    stage: "",
    round: null,
    summary: "One community, thousands of brands, and a whole lot of second-hand style. Ready to get started? Here’s how it works. In 2008, our founder Milda Mitkute was moving but had too many clothes to take with her. Justas Janauskas offered help and built a website to give away her clothes to friends. Soon enough, the media wanted in. The duo knew they were on to something – Vinted was born. Today, more than 2,000 people work from our HQ in Lithuania and offices across Europe. Our team spans countries and cultural backgrounds, just like our members. Every day, we help our members trade millions of second-hand items, going beyond clothes to include everything from kids’ items to luxury handbags. By keeping items in circulation for longer, Vinted makes it easy for the world to make the most of what we already have. Our Impact Report has proven that second-hand is better than new for the climate, for your wardrobe and for your wallet. That’s why we want to make it first choice for everyone. Vinted’s mission is backed by leading venture capital firms from both sides of the Atlantic, including Accel, Burda Principal Investments, EQT Growth, Insight Partners, Lightspeed Venture Partners, and Sprints. You can read our latest updates in the Newsroom . Get the free app and sell the clothes you just don’t wear anymore. For your price, with 0% selling fees.",
